        "original_id": "c994ed87-86fa-5bdb-ac5f-1d97f2e00ba3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: S. Truett Cathy, Mark Carman, Zach Bonner, Brandon Pugh, Thomas Smith, Michael Taggart\n- Companies: Chick-fil-A\n- Places: College Park, Georgia\n- Awards: President's Volunteer Service Award, Call to Service Award\n- Topics: Fast food, chicken sandwiches, volunteer service\n\nFacts:\n- S. Truett Cathy founded the fast food restaurant chain Chick-fil-A.\n- Chick-fil-A is an American fast food restaurant chain that specializes in chicken sandwiches.\n- Chick-fil-A is headquartered in the Atlanta district of College Park, Georgia.\n- The name Chick-fil-A is a play on the American English pronunciation of \"fillet.\"\n- The Call to Service Award is the most prestigious level of the President's Volunteer Service Award.\n- The Call to Service Award recognizes more than 4,000 hours of extraordinary service.\n- S. Truett Cathy, Mark Carman, Zach Bonner, Brandon Pugh, Thomas Smith, and Michael Taggart are among the few Americans who have received the Call to Service Award.",
